What's the matter with the captain?

78
00:04:14,040 --> 00:04:15,320
I have no idea.

79
00:04:15,660 --> 00:04:17,180
But whatever it is, it's serious.

80
00:04:17,760 --> 00:04:18,680
Yeah, no kidding.

81
00:04:19,260 --> 00:04:23,400
Maybe we're here because they need to give us special orders for going to battle with the Spade Kingdom.

82
00:04:23,900 --> 00:04:24,820
I could see that.

83
00:04:25,020 --> 00:04:26,000
Enough musing!

84
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:32,560
We have assembled you all here today for a very important meeting.

85
00:04:33,840 --> 00:04:40,860
I need you to understand that whatever happens at this table has the potential to alter the course of the entire kingdom's destiny.

86
00:04:41,400 --> 00:04:44,500
And I must ask you never to speak of it outside this room.

87
00:04:45,380 --> 00:04:47,200
Sounds like a top secret mission.

88
00:04:47,840 --> 00:04:49,520
Now then, let us begin!

89
00:04:49,520 --> 00:05:01,060
Hey, I know that old lady!

90
00:05:02,520 --> 00:05:04,700
Sorry, but I don't think I'm familiar.

91
00:05:05,280 --> 00:05:07,220
She's a nun at the church in Neon.

92
00:05:07,800 --> 00:05:09,500
I wonder what brings her here, though.

93
00:05:09,500 --> 00:05:14,600
The purpose of this gathering is to celebrate Ms. Teresa's service to the sisterhood.

94
00:05:14,800 --> 00:05:16,640
She's been with them for 15 years.

95
00:05:16,960 --> 00:05:17,400
What?

96
00:05:18,160 --> 00:05:19,320
I don't understand.

97
00:05:19,580 --> 00:05:22,780
Didn't you guys just say this meeting could affect the whole kingdom's future?

98
00:05:23,160 --> 00:05:24,460
Children are the future.

99
00:05:24,960 --> 00:05:27,240
And Ms. Teresa takes care of a group of children.

100
00:05:28,060 --> 00:05:31,460
I'm sorry, but I really don't see how I could have been any more clear than that.

101
00:05:31,720 --> 00:05:33,700
I got a couple ideas, but hey, you're the boss.

102
00:05:33,700 --> 00:05:37,740
Why exactly weren't we supposed to tell anybody else about this?

103
00:05:37,920 --> 00:05:39,900
It's not as though it's some horrible secret.

104
00:05:40,400 --> 00:05:43,520
There simply isn't any reason to tell anyone else about it.

105
00:05:44,400 --> 00:05:47,620
Ms. Teresa hates the spotlight, so we can't make this flashy.

106
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:50,200
This is the worst secret mission ever!

107
00:05:51,120 --> 00:05:52,640
Well, it is too flashy.

108
00:05:52,940 --> 00:05:54,480
I don't want all of this fanfare.

109
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:57,040
Can't a poor old woman have some peace?

110
00:05:57,760 --> 00:06:00,100
So basically, we're just here to throw her a party?

111
00:06:00,960 --> 00:06:03,540
Any particular reason you're hosting this?

112
00:06:03,700 --> 00:06:08,120
Back when we were small children, in addition to being a member of the Magic Knights,

113
00:06:08,760 --> 00:06:12,260
Ms. Teresa was also responsible for educating my sister and me.

114
00:06:12,560 --> 00:06:15,940
Oh, that's right! I think I remember you telling me about that before, sister!

115
00:06:16,680 --> 00:06:20,520
Heaven help me, you haven't changed much except for your heads getting bigger.

116
00:06:21,120 --> 00:06:22,280
Mero and Little Fuego.

117
00:06:23,540 --> 00:06:25,600
Mero? Little Fuego?

118
00:06:27,160 --> 00:06:30,780
After she finished tutoring us and left the Magic Knights, she became a sister.

119
00:06:30,780 --> 00:06:33,980
And she's been with the church for 15 years as of today.

120
00:06:34,360 --> 00:06:35,020
Right, ma'am?

121
00:06:35,740 --> 00:06:41,120
I also heard about how violently you fought to protect everyone during the kidnapping incident that occurred in Neon.

122
00:06:41,800 --> 00:06:43,200
Oh, yeah! You were awesome!

123
00:06:43,880 --> 00:06:45,200
Especially for a granny!

124
00:06:45,200 --> 00:06:49,260
Which is why we have designated this day to be a time of celebration!

125
00:06:49,800 --> 00:06:52,840
We're here to honor Sister Teresa's lifetime of accomplishments!

126
00:06:53,360 --> 00:06:56,900
And since we needed more hosts than just the two of us, we brought you along.

127
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:59,020
Okay, I think I see what this is all about.

128
00:06:59,420 --> 00:07:02,100
Yeah, you want us to help throw her a super fun party!

129
00:07:02,460 --> 00:07:04,260
We can do that. Certainly!

130
00:07:04,260 --> 00:07:05,860
Simply beautiful!

131
00:07:06,280 --> 00:07:10,500
Not your looks, obviously, because you're a hideous hag, but your spirit is simply gorgeous!

132
00:07:11,220 --> 00:07:14,200
I'm learning to comprehend that non-physical form of beauty.

133
00:07:14,760 --> 00:07:17,940
But of course, my Immaculate Being still outshines all the rest.

134
00:07:18,480 --> 00:07:21,680
I know my brother's a grown man, but do you think you could educate him too?

135
00:07:21,780 --> 00:07:22,480
He's an idiot.

136
00:07:23,160 --> 00:07:23,820
Wait a second.

137
00:07:24,420 --> 00:07:25,560
Why isn't Leo here?

138
00:07:26,160 --> 00:07:29,020
It's a party for somebody who's really important to his siblings.

139
00:07:29,600 --> 00:07:32,040
Under normal circumstances, I'd have summoned him here.

140
00:07:32,040 --> 00:07:35,440
However, he asked me to let him use this time for some extra training.

141
00:07:35,920 --> 00:07:37,300
So I was happy to oblige.

142
00:07:38,300 --> 00:07:39,660
That's a good reason.

143
00:07:40,500 --> 00:07:41,820
He's got the right idea.

144
00:07:42,320 --> 00:07:45,720
Too bad you two aren't smart enough to realize what a waste this is.

145
00:07:46,060 --> 00:07:47,580
It's only for today, ma'am.

146
00:07:47,920 --> 00:07:49,040
Please try to have fun.

147
00:07:53,900 --> 00:07:56,060
Oh, wow! Looks good!

148
00:07:56,080 --> 00:07:57,800
We hope you enjoy it, Miss Teresa.

149
00:07:58,740 --> 00:07:59,220
Oh.

150
00:07:59,220 --> 00:08:03,020
I really don't care for big, fancy meals like this.

151
00:08:03,220 --> 00:08:06,700
Perhaps it's because I've been living outside of the royal capital for so long now.

152
00:08:07,080 --> 00:08:09,860
This is exactly why I almost declined your request.

153
00:08:10,240 --> 00:08:10,820
Then again.

154
00:08:11,500 --> 00:08:12,880
Look at the food!

155
00:08:13,180 --> 00:08:13,500
Yay!

156
00:08:13,640 --> 00:08:15,100
I can't wait to eat!

157
00:08:15,100 --> 00:08:20,440
You generously offered to feed the little ones as well, and it would have been selfish of me to refuse that.

158
00:08:20,660 --> 00:08:22,420
Hey, Marie. Nice to see you again.

159
00:08:22,640 --> 00:08:23,200
Hi, Asta.

160
00:08:23,460 --> 00:08:25,080
Thanks for saving me before.

161
00:08:25,440 --> 00:08:26,860
You want to eat our lunch together?

162
00:08:27,300 --> 00:08:27,740
Sure.

163
00:08:28,420 --> 00:08:29,220
Hey, wait.

164
00:08:29,820 --> 00:08:31,300
I know that key.

165
00:08:31,660 --> 00:08:32,100
Asta!

166
00:08:32,340 --> 00:08:33,720
Don't you want some food?

167
00:08:33,840 --> 00:08:34,060
Oh.

168
00:08:34,640 --> 00:08:35,700
Of course I do.

169
00:08:36,240 --> 00:08:37,800
Everybody get in line, okay?

170
00:08:38,480 --> 00:08:38,880
Okay!

171
00:08:38,880 --> 00:08:39,280
Yay!

172
00:08:39,280 --> 00:08:42,840
Here you go. That ought to be enough to get you started.

173
00:08:43,140 --> 00:08:44,400
Thank you so much, Asta.

174
00:08:47,280 --> 00:08:48,400
What's this about?

175
00:08:49,840 --> 00:08:55,040
You may have fooled everyone else here, but it takes a lot more than a clever disguise to fool me.

176
00:08:55,480 --> 00:08:56,300
Ghosh, my boy.

177
00:08:56,960 --> 00:08:57,920
Shut it, old lady.

178
00:08:57,920 --> 00:09:03,280
I suppose you must have had a transformation wizard change your appearance to make you look like a child.

179
00:09:03,600 --> 00:09:05,760
There's someone on your squad with that skill.

180
00:09:06,060 --> 00:09:06,860
I remember.

181
00:09:08,120 --> 00:09:12,540
I went to the church to visit Marie, but then I heard there was a party at House Vermillion.

182
00:09:13,500 --> 00:09:14,480
That's why I'm here.

183
00:09:14,800 --> 00:09:17,480
Do you have some kind of problem with that, you stupid old geezer?

184
00:09:17,700 --> 00:09:19,980
I see you're still as disrespectful as ever.

185
00:09:20,400 --> 00:09:23,880
You and I both know you're only allowed to see Marie once every month.

186
00:09:24,140 --> 00:09:25,800
You've got no regard for the rules.

187
00:09:26,040 --> 00:09:27,240
It's downright shameful.

188
00:09:27,240 --> 00:09:32,460
I'm just sneaking a peek during a party that we both happen to be attending, so it doesn't count.

189
00:09:34,660 --> 00:09:36,740
I'm sorry to bring the fun to a halt.

190
00:09:36,980 --> 00:09:39,340
Oh, what? You mean the party's over already?

191
00:09:39,840 --> 00:09:41,060
No, not exactly.

192
00:09:41,600 --> 00:09:43,360
Then what's the problem?

193
00:09:43,800 --> 00:09:48,300
I demand that each and every one of you demonstrate your best party trick for Sister Teresa's entertainment.

194
00:09:48,700 --> 00:09:49,100
What?

195
00:09:57,240 --> 00:10:00,080
Now then, which one of you would like to go first?

196
00:10:02,020 --> 00:10:04,440
He wants us to do party tricks?

197
00:10:04,440 --> 00:10:06,960
Like juggling and things like that?

198
00:10:07,220 --> 00:10:09,980
Oh, man. I hope someone explains what a party trick is.

199
00:10:10,160 --> 00:10:13,080
I'm sorry. Little Fuego was never very good with words.

200
00:10:13,580 --> 00:10:15,420
I do wish he would explain himself better.

201
00:10:16,300 --> 00:10:17,920
I'm not interested in tricks.

202
00:10:18,280 --> 00:10:20,000
I'd like you to entertain the children.

203
00:10:20,780 --> 00:10:21,660
Oh, that's easy.

204
00:10:21,660 --> 00:10:23,460
Leave it to me. I'm great with kids.

205
00:10:23,460 --> 00:10:24,640
Let's get started.

206
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:31,540
Good thing I'm here. Ever since the day I was born, my infallible good looks have provided an endless spectacle for the masses who clamor to behold.

207
00:10:32,140 --> 00:10:36,560
Considering your entire existence is a party trick, this ought to be the easiest thing you've ever done.

208
00:10:36,660 --> 00:10:38,760
Just try not to break any nails, Mr. Perfect.

209
00:10:39,180 --> 00:10:41,440
I don't think I know any party tricks.

210
00:10:41,800 --> 00:10:43,020
Trust me, it wasn't.

211
00:10:43,020 --> 00:10:45,240
This reminds me of Lady Ossiere.

212
00:10:45,520 --> 00:10:48,300
In times like this, she'd always be the first one to step up.

213
00:10:49,080 --> 00:10:53,600
Anytime there was a banquet, she'd do some interesting little thing to impress us.

214
00:10:54,880 --> 00:10:56,120
I have one!

215
00:10:56,520 --> 00:10:59,300
That's wonderful, Noelle! I can't wait to see it!

216
00:10:59,480 --> 00:11:01,440
Knock our socks off! I believe in you!

217
00:11:01,780 --> 00:11:04,660
I'm about to put on a show like only royalty can.

218
00:11:05,560 --> 00:11:06,040
Ta-da!

219
00:11:08,260 --> 00:11:10,160
This is impressive, right?

220
00:11:10,160 --> 00:11:13,880
Well, if that doesn't amaze you, then nothing will.

221
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:15,760
You're amazing! Don't do that!

222
00:11:16,180 --> 00:11:17,900
I can probably whip up something.

223
00:11:18,640 --> 00:11:22,400
Pathetic. I could entertain Marie way better than any of those clowns can.

224
00:11:22,620 --> 00:11:24,140
You shut your mouth, Gauche.

225
00:11:24,420 --> 00:11:30,980
If you want my take on it, disguising yourself as a child just so you can breathe the same air as your little sister makes you the biggest clown in the room.

226
00:11:31,280 --> 00:11:32,960
Who said I wanted your take, huh?

227
00:11:33,480 --> 00:11:36,440
That's what he meant by party tricks! I know what to do!

228
00:11:36,780 --> 00:11:38,860
Hey, Noelle, could you pass me a couple of plates?

229
00:11:38,860 --> 00:11:39,920
Uh, sure.

230
00:11:40,160 --> 00:11:43,460
Ta-da!

231
00:11:45,080 --> 00:11:46,520
I'm not done yet!

232
00:11:48,860 --> 00:11:50,520
Master's so talented!

233
00:11:50,940 --> 00:11:53,880
He got the biggest reaction. Not bad, I guess.

234
00:11:53,960 --> 00:11:56,180
Oh, my. Such a bizarre routine.

235
00:11:56,540 --> 00:11:59,080
Though, there's a certain flair to how garish it is.

236
00:11:59,080 --> 00:12:07,280
Thank you all for putting on such a spectacular show for our guests.

237
00:12:07,280 --> 00:12:10,640
So, what sort of trick are you going to do for me, little fuego?

238
00:12:10,640 --> 00:12:17,120
I see. It appears I'm not going to get away with doing nothing.

239
00:12:17,120 --> 00:12:20,940
All right. Time to use the ace up my sleeve.

240
00:12:21,940 --> 00:12:23,140
Watch closely, children.

241
00:12:23,140 --> 00:12:24,500
Look at these eggs.

242
00:12:24,500 --> 00:12:35,500
I don't understand. What kind of trick is he going to do with those?

243
00:12:35,500 --> 00:12:38,600
Does he really think he can boil them like that?

244
00:12:40,760 --> 00:12:41,240
There.

245
00:12:47,180 --> 00:12:47,620
Behold!

246
00:12:47,620 --> 00:12:51,420
This is crazy! How do he cook each one of these eggs to a different temperature?

247
00:12:51,420 --> 00:12:57,780
By carefully controlling my mana, I can prepare eggs to several varieties of doneness at the same time.

248
00:12:57,780 --> 00:13:01,960
The most challenging method is what's commonly known as the hot spring style.

249
00:13:02,220 --> 00:13:06,220
The yolk of the egg should be somewhat firm while the white part maintains a gelatinous texture.

250
00:13:06,540 --> 00:13:09,600
Which means for this to work, I must adjust the temperature to exactly...

251
00:13:09,600 --> 00:13:10,500
Nobody cares.

252
00:13:10,780 --> 00:13:11,980
I beg your pardon?

253
00:13:12,520 --> 00:13:14,260
You're too serious for this, brother.

254
00:13:15,080 --> 00:13:17,200
Entertaining isn't one of your strong points.

255
00:13:17,340 --> 00:13:18,240
I suppose not.

256
00:13:18,780 --> 00:13:21,260
Give me some room. Let me show you how it's done.

257
00:13:21,640 --> 00:13:24,120
The key to a proper party trick is enthusiasm.

258
00:13:24,120 --> 00:13:32,260
They'll never forget this!

259
00:13:32,760 --> 00:13:36,460
Yes! Now tell me, children, are you having fun?

260
00:13:40,200 --> 00:13:41,940
What are they crying about?

261
00:13:42,520 --> 00:13:44,880
Still painfully oblivious, aren't you?

262
00:13:45,380 --> 00:13:48,240
I apologize for this disappointing display.

263
00:13:48,440 --> 00:13:50,580
It's not like it really comes as a surprise to me.

264
00:13:50,580 --> 00:13:54,400
After all, your personalities haven't changed in the slightest since you were children.

265
00:13:54,780 --> 00:13:57,880
Could you tell us what they were like then? Maybe a funny story or something.

266
00:13:58,080 --> 00:13:59,480
Show some respect, Asta.

267
00:13:59,740 --> 00:14:04,540
If I had to describe them, I'd say that although they were capable, they were still a real handful.

268
00:14:05,940 --> 00:14:09,580
I'll be your tutor starting today. I look forward to instructing you.

269
00:14:10,120 --> 00:14:13,480
I want to do everything I can to make myself stronger, Miss Teresa.

270
00:14:13,480 --> 00:14:16,360
So please give me the most extreme training possible.

271
00:14:16,780 --> 00:14:18,200
You're being silly, little fuego.

272
00:14:18,740 --> 00:14:20,800
It isn't possible to become strong overnight.

273
00:14:21,740 --> 00:14:24,060
He was unsatisfied with the intensity of his lessons.

274
00:14:24,680 --> 00:14:28,240
So he'd always sneak away and train on his own when he was supposed to be in bed.

275
00:14:29,100 --> 00:14:32,880
But training too hard in childhood can affect a person's mana and development.

276
00:14:33,380 --> 00:14:35,360
So I tried to get him to hold back.

277
00:14:36,120 --> 00:14:38,260
Mara was always a wild child.

278
00:14:38,260 --> 00:14:41,280
She never listened to me anyway, so I let her be.

279
00:14:41,660 --> 00:14:43,100
And she became a mighty warrior.

280
00:14:43,920 --> 00:14:47,780
I served as the tutor to this pair of troublemakers for about a decade.

281
00:14:48,200 --> 00:14:52,400
At the end of my term, little fuego was 15 years old and Mara was 17.

282
00:14:53,020 --> 00:14:56,020
I apologize for being such a difficult student, Miss Teresa.

283
00:14:56,600 --> 00:15:01,840
You let me have lots of freedom in my formative years, which is why I'm as powerful as I am today.

284
00:15:02,240 --> 00:15:03,960
So I'm very grateful to you.

285
00:15:04,500 --> 00:15:07,300
Well, that's kind of you, but I was only doing my job.

286
00:15:07,300 --> 00:15:08,980
You must be a great teacher.

287
00:15:09,360 --> 00:15:12,300
Though I bet you they were both super good fighters even when they were little.

288
00:15:12,640 --> 00:15:13,440
Oh, hardly.

289
00:15:14,080 --> 00:15:16,280
Little fuego had terrible mana control.

290
00:15:16,880 --> 00:15:20,020
Frankly, in his youth, the boy was a walking fire hazard.

291
00:15:21,180 --> 00:15:22,740
Yeah, I remember that.

292
00:15:22,980 --> 00:15:26,720
You caused tons of fires, and you cried like a baby every time.

293
00:15:28,300 --> 00:15:34,260
But do you remember the time you worked yourself into a tizzy when you were eight and accidentally set your clothes on fire?

294
00:15:34,260 --> 00:15:38,100
Now that you mention it, I think I do recall that.

295
00:15:38,460 --> 00:15:40,120
Such fond memories, aren't they, sister?

296
00:15:41,400 --> 00:15:46,000
These growing pains are to be expected for children born with extraordinary levels of mana.

297
00:15:46,700 --> 00:15:52,220
But with time and practice, their ability to control their magic naturally grows in proportion to their potential.

298
00:15:52,220 --> 00:15:53,280
I get it.

299
00:15:53,280 --> 00:15:56,080
It makes sense that I couldn't control my mana for so long.

300
00:15:56,200 --> 00:15:57,360
I was a late bloomer.

301
00:15:57,880 --> 00:16:00,440
Then having poor mana control is kind of like wetting the bed.

302
00:16:00,680 --> 00:16:04,980
For most kids, it's not a problem after about ten years old, but for some it keeps happening.

303
00:16:05,340 --> 00:16:07,600
Sometimes even until they're thirteen or fourteen.

304
00:16:07,980 --> 00:16:08,980
Yes, well put.

305
00:16:09,300 --> 00:16:10,680
That's an excellent analogy.

306
00:16:10,680 --> 00:16:13,280
It really is a lot like wetting the bed, huh?

307
00:16:13,800 --> 00:16:15,300
Master, you jerk!

308
00:16:15,980 --> 00:16:18,100
I don't even know what I did wrong!

309
00:16:18,320 --> 00:16:24,840
I can hardly imagine anybody making it through childhood without picking up a few embarrassing memories along the way.

310
00:16:25,580 --> 00:16:32,720
Speaking of embarrassing memories, one time, back when we were little, Fuego Leon broke a vase our family had had for generations.

311
00:16:33,140 --> 00:16:37,040
I couldn't bear to see my little brother punished, so I took the blame for it.

312
00:16:37,040 --> 00:16:42,400
Pardon me, dear sister. It's been many years and some of the details may have passed from your memory.

313
00:16:43,020 --> 00:16:46,060
You were the one who broke that vase and I who took the blame.

314
00:16:46,260 --> 00:16:49,880
Ah, you certainly sound convinced that what you're saying is true.

315
00:16:50,060 --> 00:16:53,020
And it's not like it was out of character for you, right?

316
00:16:53,440 --> 00:16:57,500
It was the same thing after you pilfered that magic item from Father and lost it.

317
00:16:57,880 --> 00:17:00,380
You told everyone I'd taken it and they believed you.

318
00:17:00,900 --> 00:17:02,360
That'll be enough out of you.

319
00:17:02,360 --> 00:17:08,120
Did you make room in your memory for these trifles by forgetting about all the times you swiped food from me without permission?

320
00:17:08,580 --> 00:17:11,340
Or did you think I didn't notice because I never said anything?

321
00:17:11,440 --> 00:17:12,320
That never happened.

322
00:17:12,900 --> 00:17:17,540
Once again, you were the family's constant food swiper and I the long-suffering victim.

323
00:17:18,680 --> 00:17:23,260
I'm sorry, sister, but I can't allow you to spread these falsehoods to our guests unchallenged.

324
00:17:23,720 --> 00:17:26,980
Falsehoods? You better not be calling me a liar, Fuego Leon.

325
00:17:27,280 --> 00:17:29,520
Then I must insist that you recant your lie.

326
00:17:29,520 --> 00:17:34,640
Don't think for a second that you're too grown up for me to beat another lesson into your fat head.

327
00:17:34,940 --> 00:17:36,480
Feel free to take a shot.

328
00:17:39,680 --> 00:17:41,540
What do we do, sister?

329
00:17:42,360 --> 00:17:45,000
That's how siblings are. Just let them slug it out.

330
00:17:45,740 --> 00:17:47,300
Although you, over there, Missy.

331
00:17:47,840 --> 00:17:49,000
Uh, you mean me?

332
00:17:49,340 --> 00:17:51,480
Please, throw up a quick spell to protect the kids.

333
00:17:51,740 --> 00:17:53,640
I don't want them to get hurt in this malarkey.

334
00:17:54,360 --> 00:17:55,400
Yeah, got it.

335
00:17:55,400 --> 00:18:00,800
Take a good long look, kids, and don't let yourselves grow up to be like them.

336
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:01,380
Okay.

337
00:18:02,080 --> 00:18:06,200
Two people having different versions of a childhood memory hardly seems a surprise.

338
00:18:06,780 --> 00:18:12,240
I, too, protected my dear sister quite often, but it seems all those memories have escaped her.

339
00:18:12,520 --> 00:18:14,920
What? When did you ever take the fall from me?

340
00:18:14,920 --> 00:18:19,500
I beautified a room for her once after she made a terrible mess of it.

341
00:18:19,600 --> 00:18:21,100
Man, I never would have guessed.

342
00:18:21,280 --> 00:18:22,860
That's enough of your nonsense.

343
00:18:23,320 --> 00:18:25,500
You won't embarrass me in front of Husta.

344
00:18:26,320 --> 00:18:33,940
You, do you know how many times I had to sweep the entire house after you'd been practicing magic by throwing loose flower petals all over the floor?

345
00:18:34,280 --> 00:18:36,660
Oh, come now. I'm sure it couldn't have been that many.

346
00:18:36,660 --> 00:18:40,220
I've wasted so many hours of my life cleaning up after you.

347
00:18:40,900 --> 00:18:46,440
Conflict is unbecoming to one as beautiful as myself, but your vile slander against me must not go unanswered.

348
00:18:46,860 --> 00:18:50,040
I've already heard more than enough of your excuses, brother.

349
00:18:50,540 --> 00:18:53,620
If you lack the sense to shut your mouth, then I'll do it for you.

350
00:18:54,040 --> 00:18:57,980
I've never seen mimosa like this before, but there's a first time for everything.

351
00:18:58,440 --> 00:19:00,380
I won't be holding myself back anymore.

352
00:19:02,440 --> 00:19:04,880
Good, because I've been waiting for some entertainment.

353
00:19:06,660 --> 00:19:12,320
Hey, you morons! You're gonna hurt Marie!

354
00:19:14,960 --> 00:19:16,740
Whoa, where'd a ghost come from?

355
00:19:16,940 --> 00:19:18,480
You weren't supposed to be here.

356
00:19:18,720 --> 00:19:21,260
I won't let anybody harm my sister. Got it?

357
00:19:25,600 --> 00:19:29,460
You stay out of this! It's between me and my idiot brother!

358
00:19:32,120 --> 00:19:35,560
You two need to cool it! You're taking this fight way too far!

359
00:19:36,660 --> 00:19:37,460
You're taking this fight way too far!

360
00:19:37,460 --> 00:19:38,060
You're taking this fight way too far!

361
00:19:38,060 --> 00:19:38,660
You're taking this fight way too far!

362
00:19:47,380 --> 00:19:49,100
That's enough! All of you!

363
00:19:55,420 --> 00:19:58,860
Whoa! She put a stop to all those fights in an instant!

364
00:19:58,860 --> 00:20:01,640
Now sit

365
00:20:01,640 --> 00:20:06,780
How appalling

366
00:20:06,780 --> 00:20:08,140
Of course siblings fight

367
00:20:08,140 --> 00:20:10,080
But that was too much by any measure

368
00:20:10,080 --> 00:20:12,480
I'm terribly sorry for losing my composure

369
00:20:12,480 --> 00:20:13,620
With you like that brother

370
00:20:13,620 --> 00:20:16,600
I had a less than beautiful moment too

371
00:20:16,600 --> 00:20:18,120
And you too

372
00:20:18,120 --> 00:20:21,480
Your behavior today has been well beyond mortifying

373
00:20:21,480 --> 00:20:38,860
You're in your thirties

374
00:20:38,860 --> 00:20:41,960
You have no excuse to be squabbling hard enough to leather your home

375
00:20:41,960 --> 00:20:44,160
We apologize most sincerely

376
00:20:44,160 --> 00:20:47,880
Wait one damn second you old bag

377
00:20:47,880 --> 00:20:50,260
What are you just going to stand there

378
00:20:50,260 --> 00:20:51,820
Making that smug face at me

379
00:20:51,820 --> 00:20:52,960
Oh there you are

380
00:20:52,960 --> 00:20:54,680
I was wondering where you'd landed

381
00:20:54,680 --> 00:20:56,160
You wouldn't be in trouble

382
00:20:56,160 --> 00:20:59,160
If you didn't come here without permission in the first place big brother

383
00:20:59,160 --> 00:21:01,320
If nothing else

384
00:21:01,320 --> 00:21:04,560
The fact that your sister turned out so much smarter than you is comforting

385
00:21:04,560 --> 00:21:08,040
And you two did excellent work as well

386
00:21:08,040 --> 00:21:10,620
Thank you so much for looking out for the children

387
00:21:10,620 --> 00:21:15,200
Now it's time we get on our way

388
00:21:15,200 --> 00:21:17,320
Miss Teresa leaving so soon

389
00:21:17,320 --> 00:21:19,600
I've had plenty of your company

390
00:21:19,600 --> 00:21:22,740
I apologize again for how we've conducted ourselves

391
00:21:22,740 --> 00:21:26,860
But please let us make it up to you by hosting you again

392
00:21:26,860 --> 00:21:30,380
I get the feeling you haven't done much entertaining

393
00:21:30,380 --> 00:21:32,820
Was it really that obvious?

394
00:21:34,160 --> 00:21:34,620
Indeed

395
00:21:34,620 --> 00:21:38,420
But it's still nice to know that the two of you are so eager to have me here

396
00:21:38,420 --> 00:21:40,340
So let's see

397
00:21:40,340 --> 00:21:45,020
My hundredth year of service will be in 85 years

398
00:21:45,020 --> 00:21:47,480
If you can fit me into your schedule

399
00:21:47,480 --> 00:21:48,760
That she leopard

400
00:21:48,760 --> 00:21:50,600
She's really tough, huh?

401
00:21:51,260 --> 00:21:51,820
Seriously

402
00:21:51,820 --> 00:21:54,400
She could probably take out a devil on her own

403
00:21:54,400 --> 00:22:03,120
You don't live to be an old bag like me without picking up a few tricks

404
00:22:03,120 --> 00:22:18,380
My hundredth year of service

405
00:22:18,380 --> 00:22:21,440
I'll raise it and if i'm fading about time

406
00:22:21,440 --> 00:22:24,780
I keep you literally

407
00:22:24,780 --> 00:22:27,580
No matter where I could

408
00:22:27,580 --> 00:22:29,440
Do what you need

409
00:22:29,440 --> 00:22:31,840
I change the blah

410
00:22:32,660 --> 00:22:35,600
I change the blah

411
00:22:35,600 --> 00:22:37,680
It's only that you can leave

412
00:22:37,680 --> 00:22:40,280
I die from China

413
00:22:40,280 --> 00:23:10,260
Thank you.

414
00:23:10,280 --> 00:23:14,280
Don't forget it. Don't forget it.

415
00:23:14,280 --> 00:23:20,280
Don't forget it. Don't forget it.

416
00:23:20,280 --> 00:23:22,280
Don't forget it.

417
00:23:22,280 --> 00:23:26,280
That's my heart.

418
00:23:26,280 --> 00:23:31,280
If you're here, I'm not alone.

419
00:23:40,280 --> 00:23:44,280
The one who has my heart, my mind, and soul.

420
00:23:44,280 --> 00:23:50,280
Stupid Osta! What do you mean the one who has my heart? I'm royalty, you know. Jeez.

421
00:23:50,280 --> 00:24:00,280
...

